> **18 contrasts are computed on this page** (9 on accuracy, 9 on effort and steering). At alpha = 0.05 the family-wise error rate is **~60%** — several intervals excluding zero by chance alone is the expectation, not the exception. More contrasts have already been run across findings 10–12, so the true family is larger than this page. What earns confidence is not one interval but independent measures agreeing in direction and size on the same arm, and then replicating. Read this table that way.


